# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-11, pick P26). L §4.4: "a pin whose value is the read" keeps the read's name, and a
# window written in a pin is a read of the pinned cell; L §8.2 `unknown day:` names "the cell that holds it, as its
# read names it". A def pinned to a written window (qa: dd) is named by its cell, as an input is (qd: w); so is `last`
# of an input pinned so (qc), whose hole keeps its label (w) as unpinned. qa reads pay_w on w too.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
=== m.tally
model g4_b2
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.2 (N/a, #211): a hole made from a day not yet known names it in its register, unknown day: <name>: the cell that holds it (n_cell, w), a calendar's entry (n_cal, added one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-24])), a window a rule builds, by its own text (n_rule); two at once, sorted by their text (n_two); a window value that is no hole names none (n_win)."

source card "T's card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place sav: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input pay: money PLN

input w: date

input cal: calendar

input d0: date

input d1: date

input from_day: date

input x: date

input d_fix: date

def dd: date = d_fix

def wr: date = window(d0, d1)

move pay_w: transfers
  on w
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

move pay_cal: transfers
  on add_business(from_day, 1, cal)
  leg cash from world to sav amount pay

move pay_r: transfers
  on wr
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

move pay_d: transfers
  on dd
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

move pay_x: transfers
  on x
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay

version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 100.00 PLN "the card"
  w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "the card"
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-24])]) "the card"
  d0 = 2026-05-04 "the card"
  x = 2026-01-15 "the card"
  d_fix = 2026-02-01 "the card"
  d1 = 2026-05-06 "the card"
  from_day = 2026-06-19 "the card"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"

ask qa: bal(konto, 2026-03-06) with dd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
ask qb: bal(konto, 2026-06-22) with x = add_business(from_day, 1, cal)
ask qc: last(w, 2026-06-01) < 2026-03-06 with w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
ask qd: bal(konto, 2026-03-06) with w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
ask qe: w < 2026-03-06 with w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
=== expect qa qc qd
qa: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_d" (dd) ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_w" (w) ?"date within window(2026-05-04, 2026-05-06) not precise enough for the day of pay_r" (wr)
  pinned: dd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
  unknown day: dd
  unknown day: w
  unknown day: wr
  cut 2026-01-01
qc: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for last(w, 2026-06-01) < 2026-03-06" (w)
  pinned: w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
  unknown day: w
  cut 2026-01-01
qd: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for the day of pay_w" (w) ?"date within window(2026-05-04, 2026-05-06) not precise enough for the day of pay_r" (wr)
  pinned: w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07)
  unknown day: w
  unknown day: wr
  cut 2026-01-01
